She's also an author whose
children's book is called

00:00:16.927 --> 00:00:19.110
"A Dolly for Christmas", here it is,

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.170
you can buy it today, and you should.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.245
Please welcome Kimberly Schlapman y'all.

00:00:23.245 --> 00:00:27.033
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers and claps)

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:29.350
(Kelly laughs)
(Kimberly laughs)

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.710
It was a walk-by, I like it.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:32.642
Oh my, you--

00:00:32.642 --> 00:00:34.337
(Kimberly speaks indistinctly)

00:00:34.337 --> 00:00:36.900
You always look so beautiful.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.890
You're such a light Kimberly.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.310
- Oh, Kelly, you are a light.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.180
You are a light.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.250
The first time I met you,

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.820
I was like, this woman
is different and amazing.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:46.653
- Oh my god,
(audience awes)

00:00:46.653 --> 00:00:47.530
well ditto, ditto.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.390
And you just, every time you
come on screen (Kelly laughs),

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.890
I'm like good lord.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:53.010
Well say hi to Zachary and Anya.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.036
- Hey there, how are you?

00:00:54.036 --> 00:00:54.869
- Hey Zachary, hey Anya,

00:00:54.869 --> 00:00:55.883
Great to meet you.
- Hi.

00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:57.750
- it's been so much
fun to watch you y'all.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.632
I've been sitting here in my kitchen

00:00:59.632 --> 00:01:00.465
watching y'all.

00:01:00.465 --> 00:01:02.430
It's interesting.
- (laughs) Welcome to 2020.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.540
Well I want to talk about your new book.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.960
It's about your adoption of Dolly, right?

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:08.793
- Yeah.

00:01:08.793 --> 00:01:11.180
It's about our family's story
and what all we went through,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.280
the infertility and the, just the years

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.750
of working so hard and so many prayers

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:19.050
that went up to God to
bring us another baby,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.240
and it's our story of Dolly,
- Yeah.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.650
- who came right at Christmas time.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:27.180
Daisy, my older daughter,
literally prayed for a baby

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.480
for five years.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.150
Every night, she prayed for a baby.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.070
And then, she also asked Santa
Claus for a baby one year,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.200
and then that year, I think God

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.800
and Santa Claus got together,

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.272
and Dolly Grace came, and it
was just the greatest miracle.

00:01:41.272 --> 00:01:42.932
- Oh my gosh.
(audience claps)

00:01:42.932 --> 00:01:45.080
Why did you decide to adopt,

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.790
and what was that journey like?

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.610
Tell us what that was like.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.080
- Well, we went through
some rounds of in vitro.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.040
Well, for years, we just tried naturally

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.580
to get pregnant again
after we had little Daisy,

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.750
and that never worked out.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.433
And we had some heartbreak
in there, miscarriage.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.680
And then we did two rounds of in vitro.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.710
And you know, all the
things that go with that.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.510
And there are just so many women out there

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.450
who are doing that now,
and bless you for that.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:17.450
But after many years of failure
at that and loss, losses,

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.920
we decided, well, I always to adopt.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.050
My husband and I both did.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:24.420
So we thought, you know
what, I think it's time.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.890
I think it's time we start
that adoption process.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.530
So we did, and then,

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.570
now we know what we were waiting for.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:33.230
We were waiting for little Dolly.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.530
And it's so, was worth the wait.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:38.970
- So what was it like to hold
Dolly for the first time?

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.700
I mean, all that time waiting, you know,

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.210
for your little one, and then finally.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.043
- Well there's something,

00:02:44.043 --> 00:02:47.460
I never told anybody,
but I had a secret worry

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.550
that I wouldn't love this adopted baby

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.410
like I love my Daisy, whom I carried.

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:56.380
But I'm telling you, when
I picked that child up

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:57.980
and put her in my arms,

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:01.300
the love is exactly the same.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.570
There is not a bit of
difference in the love

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:06.270
for the baby that I carried and the baby

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.660
that God gave us through adoption.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:09.190
It's exactly the same.

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:11.143
- I've actually heard several
people say that with adoption,

00:03:11.143 --> 00:03:13.110
that it was specifically the mothers

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:13.990
that were always worried.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:15.400
They were like, "I'm just
worried, because you know,

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.340
I had this other child in me,"
- Yeah.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.650
- and they always say the same thing.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.330
They say it's identical.
- Yeah.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.710
- That's a beautiful thing.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:25.300
So does your Dolly have
the kick-butt attitude

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.543
of Dolly Parton?

00:03:26.543 --> 00:03:27.950
(audience laughs)
(Kimberly laughs)

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:30.070
- She's so much fun, yes.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.990
It was my husband's
idea to name her Dolly,

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.580
which I'm so happy he thought of that.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:35.760
It was perfect.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.630
But she's funny, she's outgoing,
she's delightfully sassy,

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.930
you know, she's got the
perfect little amount of sass

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:43.790
and so much fun.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.130
And we got to meet,
those are the pictures,

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:48.370
we got to meet the Dolly.
- Oh my god.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.880
- And she was just so precious
about my little Dolly,

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:52.810
and I've seen her since,

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.540
and she always is just the sweetest.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.373
We love that woman.
- You're, oh, Dolly,

00:03:56.373 --> 00:03:58.060
yeah, Dolly Parton is
such an amazing woman.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.700
And so sweet.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.830
Your daughter, Dolly's gonna freak out

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.060
when she's older at
those pictures (laughs).

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:03.893
- Yeah, totally (laughs).

00:04:03.893 --> 00:04:07.280
- Like, I'm like, I want
those pictures, like (laughs),

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.890
that's amazing.
- You know what happened,

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.670
when my Dolly met the Dolly,

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:12.560
she kept putting her hands somewhere,

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.974
in a particular place.
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:14.974 --> 00:04:15.807
(Kimberly laughs)

00:04:15.807 --> 00:04:17.340
- It must be a baby thing though.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:18.420
My kids were like that.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:19.950
My girl and my boy.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.070
They both kept touching people's

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.790
I go, "You can't touch people's boobs."

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:23.950
Like you gotta lay off.
(Zachary laughs)

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.950
Like, it's like, they always kept trying,

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.040
and I'm like, I don't know,
they look like pillows

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.210
I guess, I don't know to a baby,

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:30.043
I don't know.
- I know.

00:04:30.043 --> 00:04:31.060
- But they, it was, yeah,

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.500
then you feel awkward when you're the mom.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.907
You're like, "They never do that."

00:04:33.907 --> 00:04:35.656
(group laughs)

00:04:35.656 --> 00:04:36.944
So you've met Dolly, right?

00:04:36.944 --> 00:04:37.910
Dolly Parton.
- I have yeah, yeah.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.160
- Is it awesome?

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:39.993
- It was amazing.

00:04:39.993 --> 00:04:42.450
We were both guests on a talk show,

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.880
and we were in the green room area.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.010
She was about to go on.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.700
I had just come off stage.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.790
So I didn't want to get, you know,

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:51.490
I was respectful of her space.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.750
But she just went like that

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.010
across the green room,
(audience laughs)

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:55.947
and I was like,

00:04:55.947 --> 00:04:56.910
"What?", like,
- Stop.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.560
- so, I had this incredible
interaction with her.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.840
I didn't take a picture,
which I feel like,

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.132
I'm not big on like, "Can
we take a picture?", like,

00:05:04.132 --> 00:05:05.230
- I don't like bothering people either.

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.640
- but that's one person
that I've met in my life

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.604
where I'm like, "Why didn't I just

00:05:09.604 --> 00:05:10.437
pull out my phone?"
- I know,

00:05:10.437 --> 00:05:11.430
but that's such a cool experience.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.477
Of course she did this

00:05:12.477 --> 00:05:13.610
from far away.
- I love the memory.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:14.810
The memory is enough,
- That's amazing.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.850
- and just that image of
her being so thoughtful

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.763
and so generous.
- Oh, she's so kind.

00:05:19.763 --> 00:05:20.800
Agreed.
- She's amazing.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.860
- Well, Kimberly's book is
called "A Dolly for Christmas".

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.110
It's out right now,
y'all gotta check it out.

